Heap is a type of complete binary tree that follows a specific ordering between parent and child nodes.
it is mainly used to efficiently find the maximum or minimum element.
types of heaps
========================
there are  2 types of heaps
1.maxheap
===========================
parent node is always greater than or equal to its children.
the largest element is always the root.

min heap
=============================
parent node is always smaller than its children
the smallest element is always be the root

formulas
=================
parent---(i-1)/2
left child-----2*i+1
right child----------2*i+2;

4. Basic Operations
Operation	         Time Complexity
Insert               	O(log n)
Delete root         	O(log n)
Get Min/Max	            O(1)
Heapify	              O(log n)
Build Heap              O(n)
Search	                O(n)

